; Leg HK -- edit 21 on the wire.  --safe-server forces FILE COLLISION to
; RENAME for the whole session (ckcpro.c:503), so this path is NOT optional.
;
; TWO TARGET NAME LENGTHS, because znewn() picks its branch by LENGTH and the
; control failed differently in each:
;     4 chars  -> D:\HK.D.~1~, DOS refuses it, E PACKET WITH EMPTY TEXT
;                 before any data.  The existing file survives.
;     9 chars  -> branch B's sprintf lands past the string's own terminator,
;                 the name comes back UNCHANGED, and the server SILENTLY
;                 OVERWRITES the existing file.
;
; EACH NAME IS SENT TWICE.  The second send is the one under test.
;
; THE DISK IS THE OBSERVABLE AND THE F-PACKET ACK IS NOT.  ckcpro.w:1546
; sends fspec, which rcvfil() fills from the incoming name BEFORE the
; collision switch runs -- SS16bb leg MB's ACKs said rcvmb.dat while the file
; on disk was RCVMB.001.  Read the answer with:
;     vtg_image_util list <img>:1:
;
; PASS: RCVHK.DAT and HK.D still hold the FIRST fixture, RCVHK.001 and
; HK.001 hold the second, no E packet anywhere, coll=1 on the .OUT.

set speed 38400
set receive timeout 20
set parity none
set prefixing cautious
set block 3
set retry 30
set carrier-watch off
log packets s16bcHK.pkt
send rcvhk1.dat rcvhk.dat
send rcvhk1.dat hk.d
send rcvhk2.dat rcvhk.dat
send rcvhk2.dat hk.d
finish
statistics
